1
00:00:03,620 --> 00:00:05,260
[BERTHOLDT]
Heads up. She's back.

2
00:00:05,290 --> 00:00:06,920
Good.

3
00:00:09,290 --> 00:00:10,930
[REINER grunts]

4
00:00:23,740 --> 00:00:26,140
Oh, no!

5
00:00:26,180 --> 00:00:29,910
[ARMIN] No! They're
getting away with Eren!

6
00:00:36,490 --> 00:00:38,290
[Grunts]

7
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:41,460
Ride! Let the Titans chase you!

8
00:00:41,490 --> 00:00:44,330
All squads, follow my lead!

9
00:00:44,360 --> 00:00:48,030
Do what? Erwin,
you conniving bastard!

10
00:00:48,100 --> 00:00:50,400
You're using us as bait again?

11
00:00:50,440 --> 00:00:52,170
It's the only way!

12
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:57,540
You've fought well as MP's.
Now give your all as soldiers!

13
00:00:57,610 --> 00:01:00,940
The Armored Titan must
be stopped before he takes Eren.

14
00:01:00,980 --> 00:01:03,650
Failure is not an option!

15
00:01:05,550 --> 00:01:10,550
♪ Opening Song ♪

16
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:49,340
Reiner's too slow!
We've got him!

17
00:02:49,370 --> 00:02:51,540
I won't hesitate this time.

18
00:02:51,570 --> 00:02:53,870
I'll kill them
without a thought.

19
00:02:53,910 --> 00:02:56,340
If Ymir feels
like getting in the way,

20
00:02:56,380 --> 00:02:58,580
so much the worse for her.

21
00:02:58,680 --> 00:03:03,080
This ends here and now.
I swear it!

22
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:16,900
[Coughing]

23
00:03:16,930 --> 00:03:18,660
[BERTHOLDT]
Christa!

24
00:03:24,570 --> 00:03:25,910
[CHRISTA gasps]

25
00:03:25,940 --> 00:03:27,870
Ymir.

26
00:03:34,950 --> 00:03:36,420
Ymir!

27
00:03:36,450 --> 00:03:40,390
[Coughs]

28
00:03:40,420 --> 00:03:41,450
Christa--

29
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:42,720
[Coughing]

30
00:03:42,760 --> 00:03:50,260
No--Historia,
I'm sorry about eating you.

31
00:03:50,300 --> 00:03:53,330
You're uh, probably pissed.

32
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:54,770
[Coughs]

33
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:57,970
Wha-What is this? I--

34
00:03:58,010 --> 00:04:00,340
What's going on? Talk to me!

35
00:04:00,410 --> 00:04:01,770
We came to rescue you and Er--

36
00:04:01,810 --> 00:04:03,680
Just shut up!

37
00:04:03,750 --> 00:04:07,180
I don't need rescuing.
Things have changed.

38
00:04:07,250 --> 00:04:09,880
I'm with Reiner
and Bertholdt now.

39
00:04:09,950 --> 00:04:12,690
Like it or not,
you're coming with us.

40
00:04:12,750 --> 00:04:16,160
There's no future
inside the walls.

41
00:04:16,190 --> 00:04:18,520
[Panting]

42
00:04:18,590 --> 00:04:21,660
Here me out
for a second, okay?

43
00:04:21,700 --> 00:04:25,530
Life outside isn't as bad
as you think, believe me.

44
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:28,600
For starters, there's no one
saying the world woulda be

45
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:32,940
a better place
if you'd never been born.

46
00:04:32,970 --> 00:04:36,140
Yeah, I don't think Titans
would say much either way.

47
00:04:36,180 --> 00:04:39,010
They'd be too busy
trying to devour me!

48
00:04:39,050 --> 00:04:40,380
We've all got flaws!

49
00:04:40,450 --> 00:04:42,350
They're not so bad if
you'd just give 'em a break!

50
00:04:42,380 --> 00:04:45,150
It's complicated, all right?
Get off your high horse!

51
00:04:45,190 --> 00:04:47,690
Ymir! I don't know what's
going on in your mind,

52
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:51,160
but you're not making
any sense! Come on!

53
00:04:51,190 --> 00:04:53,190
What did Reiner
and Bertholdt say?

54
00:04:53,230 --> 00:04:54,690
You're doing this
against your will,

55
00:04:54,730 --> 00:04:56,800
they threatened you!

56
00:05:02,500 --> 00:05:05,540
It's the opposite, actually.

57
00:05:05,570 --> 00:05:08,040
I'm right, aren't I? Let go!

58
00:05:08,080 --> 00:05:10,240
Whatever they've got
on you, I don't care!

59
00:05:10,310 --> 00:05:12,250
We can fight them!

60
00:05:12,310 --> 00:05:14,180
Put the past behind you!

61
00:05:14,220 --> 00:05:16,380
What matters is right now!

62
00:05:16,480 --> 00:05:20,320
I'm here! I will
always be your ally!

63
00:05:26,590 --> 00:05:28,930
[BERTHOLDT]
Ymir!

64
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:31,760
Look. In case you
haven't noticed,

65
00:05:31,830 --> 00:05:33,770
the Scouts are closing in.

66
00:05:33,840 --> 00:05:36,070
If we'd left earlier,
there might've been

67
00:05:36,170 --> 00:05:38,600
a decent chance
of outrunning them.

68
00:05:38,670 --> 00:05:40,940
Going back for Christa
was your idea.

69
00:05:41,010 --> 00:05:44,740
You forced us. Remember that.

70
00:05:44,780 --> 00:05:48,550
We waited.
For what? Damn it, Ymir!

71
00:05:48,580 --> 00:05:50,780
What the hell
did we do this for?

72
00:05:50,850 --> 00:05:53,220
You can't have
a change of heart!

73
00:05:53,250 --> 00:05:55,390
You want her
to rot inside the walls?

74
00:05:55,420 --> 00:05:58,120
Does that seem
acceptable to you now?

75
00:05:58,190 --> 00:06:00,760
Don't be a fool! Think!

76
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:03,760
Let go! Don't listen to him!

77
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:05,830
I can't!

78
00:06:12,240 --> 00:06:14,870
I wish I could.

79
00:06:14,910 --> 00:06:16,910
I'm sorry, sweetie.

80
00:06:16,950 --> 00:06:20,050
I know you think
I did this for you.

81
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:23,680
But at the end of the day,
I did it for me.

82
00:06:27,260 --> 00:06:30,290
A long time ago I stole
the Power of the Titans

83
00:06:30,330 --> 00:06:32,590
from one of their comrades.

84
00:06:32,630 --> 00:06:34,630
Not much I can do against them.

85
00:06:34,660 --> 00:06:38,000
Sooner or later, I'm screwed.

86
00:06:38,070 --> 00:06:42,900
But, they said if
I cooperate, hand you over,

87
00:06:42,940 --> 00:06:45,570
maybe I've got
a shot at leniency.

88
00:06:45,640 --> 00:06:48,410
Maybe my crime gets overlooked.

89
00:06:48,440 --> 00:06:50,640
You're crucial to the Church.

90
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:52,780
You know the truth
about the walls!

91
00:06:52,810 --> 00:06:54,510
[Gasps]

92
00:06:54,580 --> 00:06:58,450
[CHRISTA] My family?
That's it, isn't it?

93
00:06:58,490 --> 00:07:01,920
[YMIR]
Sure. Why not?

94
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:04,790
[YMIR] When this world
started going to hell

95
00:07:04,830 --> 00:07:07,190
I thought to myself,
"couldn't hurt to have

96
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:10,100
a bargaining chip
in my back pocket."

97
00:07:10,130 --> 00:07:13,830
The castle's as close
to death as I ever wanna get.

98
00:07:13,870 --> 00:07:16,300
Whole experience
traumatized me.

99
00:07:16,340 --> 00:07:18,140
Gave me perspective.

100
00:07:18,170 --> 00:07:20,510
If I have to play
dirty to stay alive,

101
00:07:20,540 --> 00:07:22,140
then I have to play dirty.

102
00:07:22,180 --> 00:07:26,180
Pathetic, yeah. Doesn't make
me the ideal friend.

103
00:07:26,210 --> 00:07:31,450
Like I said, though,
I didn't do this for you.

104
00:07:31,490 --> 00:07:34,320
You deserve better,
but there it is.

105
00:07:36,990 --> 00:07:39,960
I need you.

106
00:07:39,990 --> 00:07:42,800
Please save me, Historia!

107
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:52,740
[CHRISTA]
Well, like I said.

108
00:07:52,810 --> 00:07:55,570
[Gasps]

109
00:07:55,640 --> 00:08:00,850
I'm here, and I will
always be your ally!

110
00:08:04,250 --> 00:08:06,750
[YMIR sobs]

111
00:08:17,900 --> 00:08:19,570
[grunts, yells]

112
00:08:30,280 --> 00:08:32,080
[MALE SOLDIER 36A screams]

113
00:08:34,250 --> 00:08:37,050
[Roars]

114
00:08:38,850 --> 00:08:40,220
[MIKASA grunts]

115
00:08:40,250 --> 00:08:42,860
Reiner! Protect us!

116
00:08:42,890 --> 00:08:44,720
[MIKASA grunts]

117
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:55,400
[YMIR TITAN roars]

118
00:08:55,440 --> 00:08:59,140
[MIKASA] All right, then.
Looks like Ymir goes first!

119
00:08:59,210 --> 00:09:01,440
--[MIKASA bellows]
--[CHRISTA] Mikasa, no!

120
00:09:04,280 --> 00:09:05,980
You're not going to kill Ymir.

121
00:09:06,050 --> 00:09:09,580
That all depends on her.
What'll it be?

122
00:09:09,620 --> 00:09:12,280
She can step aside
or she can die. Her choice.

123
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:14,490
That's not fair!
She'll die if she doesn't

124
00:09:14,560 --> 00:09:17,290
go along with what Reiner
and Bertholdt tell her to do.

125
00:09:17,330 --> 00:09:19,290
She's screwed either way!

126
00:09:19,330 --> 00:09:21,990
[Grunts] Listen,
there're only so many lives

127
00:09:22,060 --> 00:09:24,060
I can give a damn about.

128
00:09:24,100 --> 00:09:28,430
Cruel, but that's the world our
enemies gave us six years ago.

129
00:09:28,470 --> 00:09:30,770
Sorry. I don't have
any heartstrings left

130
00:09:30,810 --> 00:09:35,010
for you to tug on. If you
want compassion, move on.

131
00:09:35,080 --> 00:09:37,740
You want fair, tough shit.

132
00:09:37,780 --> 00:09:41,380
Time's wasting.
Pick your side, Christa.

133
00:09:41,420 --> 00:09:45,450
Eren? Or the bitch
I'm gonna kill?

134
00:09:45,490 --> 00:09:46,620
[Roars]

135
00:09:46,650 --> 00:09:48,390
[CHRISTA]
Ymir, stop!

136
00:09:48,460 --> 00:09:50,760
Look at her face! She means it!

137
00:09:50,790 --> 00:09:52,760
Don't make a move!

138
00:10:00,270 --> 00:10:02,670
[EREN grunts]

139
00:10:02,700 --> 00:10:05,970
Quit struggling!
It's not going to help!

140
00:10:06,010 --> 00:10:08,670
[JEAN] Good luck talking sense
into that one, Bertholdt.

141
00:10:08,710 --> 00:10:11,610
When something lights
a fire under him, that's it.

142
00:10:11,650 --> 00:10:14,110
Getting Eren to
calm down's a lost cause.

143
00:10:14,180 --> 00:10:15,980
Take my word for it.

144
00:10:16,020 --> 00:10:18,450
I've been on the receiving
end more than you have.

145
00:10:18,490 --> 00:10:21,320
What do you say
we teach him patience?

146
00:10:21,360 --> 00:10:23,620
Come on. Show yourself.

147
00:10:23,660 --> 00:10:25,720
Give him back! Right now!

148
00:10:25,790 --> 00:10:30,460
[CONNY] Guys, really? This is
some kind of joke, right?

149
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:32,130
No way this is you.

150
00:10:32,170 --> 00:10:34,230
You've been lying
to us this whole time?

151
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:36,140
We were supposed to be comrades!

152
00:10:36,170 --> 00:10:40,070
They still are! This is all
just a misunderstanding!

153
00:10:43,710 --> 00:10:45,380
[JEAN]
Where d'you think you're going?

154
00:10:45,410 --> 00:10:47,980
You can't keep running forever.

155
00:10:48,020 --> 00:10:51,380
We're not gonna let
that happen. Rat bastards.

156
00:10:51,420 --> 00:10:53,420
Through thick and thin
we slept under the same roof

157
00:10:53,490 --> 00:10:55,390
as soldiers for three years.

158
00:10:55,420 --> 00:10:58,160
Matter of fact, the
positions you could sleep in

159
00:10:58,190 --> 00:11:00,690
were an art from, Bertholdt.

160
00:11:00,730 --> 00:11:03,030
I'm not kidding.
We all loved waking up

161
00:11:03,060 --> 00:11:05,200
to see your contortions
in the morning.

162
00:11:05,230 --> 00:11:08,530
Used to predict
the weather with 'em.

163
00:11:08,570 --> 00:11:10,740
How'd you do it, Bertholdt?

164
00:11:10,770 --> 00:11:13,040
Must not've had
a care in the world.

165
00:11:13,070 --> 00:11:17,940
Lying beside your victims,
yet you slept like a log.

166
00:11:18,010 --> 00:11:20,550
Was it all just an act to you?

167
00:11:20,580 --> 00:11:22,110
What about the way
we used to talk about

168
00:11:22,180 --> 00:11:24,220
surviving this together?

169
00:11:24,250 --> 00:11:27,920
About growing old, looking back
on the worst of it over drinks.

170
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:31,920
Remember? Was that all bullshit?

171
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:33,860
Answer me!

172
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:38,560
Go on. What was the point?
What were you trying to do?

173
00:11:38,600 --> 00:11:41,130
[MIKASA]
It doesn't matter anymore.

174
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:44,870
Shut up and focus on
opening the traitor's neck.

175
00:11:44,910 --> 00:11:48,940
Hesitate for a moment
and we forfeit Eren.

176
00:11:48,980 --> 00:11:51,280
Who cares
what they pretended to be?

177
00:11:51,310 --> 00:11:53,410
This was their choice.

178
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:56,920
No! You're wrong!

179
00:11:56,950 --> 00:12:01,190
Who chooses to be this? Tell me!

180
00:12:04,590 --> 00:12:07,930
What d'you think I am?
Huh? What?

181
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:11,660
You think this is
what we aspired to be?

182
00:12:11,730 --> 00:12:15,170
People loathe us.
And why wouldn't they?

183
00:12:15,240 --> 00:12:16,900
We're monsters!

184
00:12:16,940 --> 00:12:21,810
We deserve to die
for the things we've done.

185
00:12:21,840 --> 00:12:24,780
We're lost. We could live
a thousand years

186
00:12:24,810 --> 00:12:27,410
and never again know peace.

187
00:12:27,450 --> 00:12:29,780
Try to imagine that darkness.

188
00:12:29,820 --> 00:12:33,290
The only light was
our brief time as soldiers.

189
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:36,920
It was never a lie!
Do you understand?

190
00:12:36,960 --> 00:12:40,590
We're not who we said we were,
but it wasn't an act!

191
00:12:40,630 --> 00:12:45,000
We genuinely thought
of you as our friends!

192
00:12:45,030 --> 00:12:49,540
I'm not stupid. I know I have
no right to ask forgiveness,

193
00:12:49,600 --> 00:12:54,640
but please. I beg of you.

194
00:12:54,680 --> 00:13:00,850
If we were comrades,
someone find us.

195
00:13:05,720 --> 00:13:10,360
Give him back.
I won't ask again.

196
00:13:10,390 --> 00:13:13,160
I'm sorry. I can't.

197
00:13:13,190 --> 00:13:14,530
[MIKASA gasps]

198
00:13:14,560 --> 00:13:16,830
[BERTHOLDT]
One of you has to do it.

199
00:13:16,860 --> 00:13:21,670
One of you has to stain
your hands with my blood!

200
00:13:21,700 --> 00:13:26,310
[HANNES] Guys! Get down
from there and take cover!

201
00:13:26,340 --> 00:13:27,870
What the hell's Erwin doing?

202
00:13:27,910 --> 00:13:30,880
He's off his rocker! Look!

203
00:13:31,650 --> 00:13:33,110
The lunatic's leading
the Titans straight for us!

204
00:13:49,430 --> 00:13:51,290
[REINER TITAN growls lowly]

205
00:13:54,600 --> 00:13:58,070
Jump, damn you!
Get the hell out of there!

206
00:13:59,570 --> 00:14:03,640
Squadrons break!
Make the Titans scatter!

207
00:14:09,110 --> 00:14:10,910
[REINER TITAN grunts]

208
00:14:12,550 --> 00:14:13,750
[CHRISTA grunts]

209
00:14:13,780 --> 00:14:15,320
[BOTH groan]

210
00:14:22,660 --> 00:14:24,830
--[CHRISTA screams]
--[YMIR] Historia!

211
00:14:27,760 --> 00:14:33,530
[Roars]

212
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:37,710
[JEAN]
What's going on? Is this hell?

213
00:14:39,380 --> 00:14:41,980
[ERWIN]
Not yet. But it will be.

214
00:14:42,010 --> 00:14:44,650
All soldiers charge!

215
00:14:44,680 --> 00:14:45,980
[CONNY]
Huh?

216
00:14:46,020 --> 00:14:48,280
[ERWIN] We've come
to the moment of truth!

217
00:14:48,320 --> 00:14:51,020
Mankind's fate is decided now!

218
00:14:51,090 --> 00:14:52,550
There is no future in which

219
00:14:52,620 --> 00:14:54,720
we reclaim these lands
without Eren--

220
00:14:54,790 --> 00:14:56,490
and there never will be!

221
00:14:56,530 --> 00:15:00,990
Go! Recover Eren from
the Armored Titan and retreat!

222
00:15:01,030 --> 00:15:04,360
Your heart and soul
to the cause!

223
00:15:05,170 --> 00:15:06,830
[CONNY]
Mikasa, wait!

224
00:15:10,140 --> 00:15:14,410
[SCOUTS yell]

225
00:15:14,480 --> 00:15:16,540
[MALE SOLDIER 33B]
This is madness.

226
00:15:16,580 --> 00:15:19,310
The Scouts have taken one
too many hits to the skull.

227
00:15:19,350 --> 00:15:21,080
--Look out!
--Huh?

228
00:15:21,150 --> 00:15:22,550
[MALE SOLDIER 33B screams]

229
00:15:27,090 --> 00:15:28,720
[EREN]
What's happening out there?

230
00:15:28,790 --> 00:15:31,290
Ugh! If only I could see!

231
00:15:34,760 --> 00:15:38,700
[REINER] I can't move. 'Less I
can shake these Titans,

232
00:15:38,730 --> 00:15:42,240
it'll only get worse.

233
00:15:42,270 --> 00:15:45,710
Okay, then.
Heads up, Bertholdt.

234
00:15:45,740 --> 00:15:47,840
Brace yourself!

235
00:15:47,880 --> 00:15:51,950
That's right.
Just a little more!

236
00:15:52,010 --> 00:15:54,880
It's working!
His hands are down!

237
00:15:54,920 --> 00:15:56,250
Now's our chance!

238
00:15:56,290 --> 00:15:59,250
Uh, Mikasa? You can see
those Titans, right?

239
00:15:59,360 --> 00:16:01,220
I mean, I get it, you're strong.

240
00:16:01,260 --> 00:16:03,060
But that's one hell of a mess.

241
00:16:03,090 --> 00:16:05,830
Slipping through
isn't gonna be easy.

242
00:16:05,900 --> 00:16:07,930
Advance!

243
00:16:09,130 --> 00:16:10,730
[MIKASA gasps]

244
00:16:11,870 --> 00:16:13,870
[ALL gasp]

245
00:16:13,900 --> 00:16:17,600
[MALE SOLDIER 36C]
Commander Erwin!

246
00:16:18,370 --> 00:16:21,810
I said advance, goddamn it!

247
00:16:21,880 --> 00:16:26,550
Eren's right in front
of you! Do not falter!

248
00:16:26,580 --> 00:16:28,220
[Gasps]

249
00:16:32,320 --> 00:16:34,250
[SCOUTS yell]

250
00:16:34,290 --> 00:16:35,890
[MALE SOLDIER 36D screams]

251
00:16:35,930 --> 00:16:38,460
[MALE SOLDIER 36E and 36F scream]

252
00:16:38,490 --> 00:16:41,900
--[MALE SOLDIER 36G screams]
--[MALE SOLDIER 36H yells]

253
00:16:41,930 --> 00:16:43,600
[MALE SOLDIER 36I screams]

254
00:16:43,630 --> 00:16:47,470
[ALL yell]

255
00:16:56,080 --> 00:16:57,950
[MIKASA grunts]

256
00:16:59,950 --> 00:17:04,250
[EREN yells muffled]

257
00:17:04,790 --> 00:17:06,420
[Screams]

258
00:17:06,460 --> 00:17:08,690
[JEAN]
Mikasa!

259
00:17:08,760 --> 00:17:12,630
You piece of shit!
Get your hands off her!

260
00:17:14,530 --> 00:17:18,470
[MALE SOLDIER 36K, 36L yell]

261
00:17:19,670 --> 00:17:22,040
We've come too far
to give up now.

262
00:17:22,100 --> 00:17:26,270
Wearegoing home.
And Eren is coming with us.

263
00:17:26,310 --> 00:17:29,110
[EREN]
No. This is all on me.

264
00:17:29,140 --> 00:17:32,050
People are dying
because I got caught!

265
00:17:32,110 --> 00:17:33,480
[ARMIN]
Bertholdt!

266
00:17:35,820 --> 00:17:38,250
[EREN]
Armin?

267
00:17:40,190 --> 00:17:42,660
[ARMIN]
That's the irony, really.

268
00:17:42,690 --> 00:17:45,990
If you can't let it go
it's not worth holding on to.

269
00:17:46,030 --> 00:17:48,630
[ERWIN]
Advance!

270
00:17:49,670 --> 00:17:54,330
[ARMIN] Think. What is it
I have to let go of?

271
00:17:54,370 --> 00:17:59,310
My life? Or something else?

272
00:18:00,480 --> 00:18:02,440
[Gasps]

273
00:18:17,890 --> 00:18:21,760
[ARMIN]
So, you're okay with this?

274
00:18:21,830 --> 00:18:25,200
Leaving your friend behind
to face the music?

275
00:18:25,230 --> 00:18:26,530
[BERTHOLDT gasps]

276
00:18:26,570 --> 00:18:28,370
[REINER gasps]

277
00:18:28,400 --> 00:18:31,170
I guess Annie
was weighing you down?

278
00:18:31,210 --> 00:18:33,010
D'you know where she is?

279
00:18:33,040 --> 00:18:38,380
Way up north in the Utopia
District. Being tortured.

280
00:18:38,410 --> 00:18:40,010
[grunts]

281
00:18:40,050 --> 00:18:43,050
[ARMIN] The silent treatment
only goes so far.

282
00:18:43,090 --> 00:18:47,250
The body may heal, but her
screams are an object lesson

283
00:18:47,320 --> 00:18:49,720
on the limits of endurance.

284
00:18:49,760 --> 00:18:52,190
Oh, don't worry,
they're taking special care

285
00:18:52,230 --> 00:18:55,700
she doesn't die...
or get a moment's rest.

286
00:18:55,730 --> 00:18:59,100
So many methods, so little time.

287
00:18:59,130 --> 00:19:01,800
Mustn't waste a
prize specimen like Annie.

288
00:19:01,870 --> 00:19:04,000
She's too precious.

289
00:19:04,040 --> 00:19:07,810
Shut your mouth, hell spawn!
I'll kill you!

290
00:19:07,880 --> 00:19:09,680
[ERWIN grunts]

291
00:19:10,910 --> 00:19:13,280
[Growls]

292
00:19:28,100 --> 00:19:31,430
[ERWIN]
All soldiers, retreat!

293
00:19:31,500 --> 00:19:34,430
[Roars]

294
00:19:36,810 --> 00:19:39,410
[Yells]

295
00:19:45,610 --> 00:19:47,480
[CHRISTA]
I did it.

296
00:19:47,520 --> 00:19:50,380
I actually killed one.
You all right?

297
00:19:50,420 --> 00:19:52,150
Get away from her!

298
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:55,920
What the hell
were you trying to pull?

299
00:19:55,960 --> 00:19:57,320
We're leaving!

300
00:19:57,360 --> 00:19:59,160
Yeah, couldn't you go for
some grub right about now?

301
00:19:59,190 --> 00:20:02,000
You don't understand!
Let me down!

302
00:20:02,030 --> 00:20:03,060
Please!

303
00:20:03,100 --> 00:20:04,360
[BOTH]
Huh?

304
00:20:04,430 --> 00:20:06,170
Reiner and Bertholdt
are going to kill Ymir

305
00:20:06,200 --> 00:20:08,870
unless we both agree
to go back with them!

306
00:20:08,940 --> 00:20:11,810
She'll only be free
if she hands me over!

307
00:20:11,840 --> 00:20:16,440
I'd already decided
to let that happen.

308
00:20:16,480 --> 00:20:18,810
Are you nuts?
What if it's a trick?

309
00:20:18,850 --> 00:20:21,050
[CHRISTA]
It's not! Let me go!

310
00:20:21,120 --> 00:20:23,820
Conny's right!
Whatever she said, it's a lie!

311
00:20:23,850 --> 00:20:26,290
Don't listen to her!

312
00:20:26,320 --> 00:20:27,950
This doesn't make sense.

313
00:20:27,990 --> 00:20:29,460
Why would someone
who fought tooth and nail

314
00:20:29,490 --> 00:20:31,730
to save your life just
turn you over to the enemy?

315
00:20:31,790 --> 00:20:33,960
What's the end game?

316
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:38,700
[CONNY] The only time Ymir
bothers to make an effort

317
00:20:38,730 --> 00:20:40,730
is when you're in danger.

318
00:20:40,800 --> 00:20:43,000
I don't know what kind
of trouble she's in,

319
00:20:43,040 --> 00:20:46,240
but for now just calm down
till we know more.

320
00:20:46,310 --> 00:20:49,210
[SASHA] Exactly. Either way,
we can't stick around.

321
00:20:49,280 --> 00:20:50,840
Whatever Ymir needs you for,
I'm sure you won't

322
00:20:50,880 --> 00:20:52,850
be much good to her dead!

323
00:20:52,880 --> 00:20:54,680
[CHRISTA gasps]

324
00:20:54,720 --> 00:20:58,820
Damn straight. Even I
could figure that one out.

325
00:20:59,660 --> 00:21:00,720
[BOTH gasp]

326
00:21:00,760 --> 00:21:03,160
[SASHA yells]

327
00:21:05,060 --> 00:21:06,560
[ALL gasp]

328
00:21:06,600 --> 00:21:09,460
[SCOUTS yell]

329
00:21:12,330 --> 00:21:14,500
He's tossing Titans now?

330
00:21:14,540 --> 00:21:18,040
That son of a bitch
has gone berserk!

331
00:21:18,070 --> 00:21:20,870
[REINER TITAN roars]

332
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:29,250
[BOTH gasp]

333
00:21:29,280 --> 00:21:31,550
[ARMIN]
Eren! Mikasa!

334
00:21:35,190 --> 00:21:36,690
Eren.

335
00:21:36,760 --> 00:21:38,590
[Whimpers]

336
00:21:40,900 --> 00:21:43,400
[Grunts and gasps]

337
00:22:10,260 --> 00:22:15,230
♪ Closing Song ♪
